      <h2>About Salaam Cave Turtle Aquarium</h2>
      <p>Salaam Cave in Kizimkazi Dimbani is a natural coral limestone cave system with tidal pools where rescued sea turtles are rehabilitated in a semi-natural environment before release. Visitors can swim, snorkel, and feed turtles in crystal-clear tidal water under guidance of local conservationists. The cave&#x27;s unique geology — freshwater lens floating on saltwater — creates a unique habitat. Community-run project supports turtle conservation and local employment. Combine with ethical dolphin tour and 12th-century Kizimkazi Mosque visit.</p>

